1
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:26,000
A Much Married Woman Who Drifts From Husband to Husband!

2
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:46,000
The Pumpkin Eater is a drama film directed by Jack Clayton.

3
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:06,000
Jo, the mother of seven children, divorces her second husband in order to
marry Jake, a successful but promiscuous screenwriter.

4
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:26,000
Though they are physically and emotionally
compatible, they are slowly torn apart.

5
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:46,000
Jo Armitage, played by Anne Bancroft.

6
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Jake Armitage, played by Peter Finch.

7
00:51:20,000 --> 00:51:26,000
Bob Conway, played by James Mason.

8
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:46,000
Beth Conway, played by Janine Gray.

9
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Mr. James - Jo's father, played by Cedric Hardwicke.

10
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:26,000
Mrs. James - Jo's mother, played by Rosalind Atkinson.

11
01:20:40,000 --> 01:20:46,000
The Pumpkin Eater is a 1964 British drama film directed by Jack
Clayton and starring Anne Bancroft and Peter Finch.

12
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
The film was adapted by Harold Pinter from the 1962 novel
of the same title by Penelope Mortimer.

13
01:35:20,000 --> 01:35:26,000
The title is a reference to the nursery rhyme "Peter Peter Pumpkin Eater".

14
01:42:40,000 --> 01:42:46,000
The tone is emotional.
